 MV (move command)
 
 mv command is used to move or rename the files and dir's
 
 Syntax: mv <source> <destination>
 
 How to rename the file?
 
 mv <file1> <file2>
 
 ex: mv  file1.txt file2.txt
 
 Above command will rename the file file1.txt to file2.txt
 
 How to move a file to a diff location?
 
 mv /home/oem/batch14/bath15/file1.txt .

 Above command will move the file file1.txt to a pwd
 
 mv /home/oem/batch14/bath15/file4.txt /home/oem/batch14
 
 Above command will move the file file4.txt form the path /home/oem/batch14/bath15/ to /home/oem/batch14
 
 .........................................
 
 CP (command command)
 
 cp command is used to copy the files and dir's from one location to another location
 
 Syntax: cp <source> <destination>
 
 How to copy a file to a diff location?
 
 cp /home/oem/batch14/bath15/file1.txt .

 Above command will copy the file file1.txt to a pwd
 
 cp /home/oem/batch14/bath15/file4.txt /home/oem/batch14
 
 Above command will copy the file file4.txt form the path /home/oem/batch14/bath15/ to /home/oem/batch14
 
 How to copy a dir and its content from one location to another location?
 
 cp -r <source-path> <destination-path>
 
 .........................................
 
 How to check the details of a command
 
 Syntax: command --help
 
 ex: cp --help
 
 
